	(text_box "VCAP_S_TAP input: 100 kOhm + 10 nF, OPA388 zero-drift follower (feeds the ADC and the OVP comparator)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(size 181.35 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8aed700a-4df4-5666-a662-d895520f5699")
	)
	(text_box "VCAP_S_TAP = Vcap x 39.8 k / (39.84 M + 39.8 k) = Vcap / 1,002.0 (string on 11; contract says 1:1,000). 1,950 V -> 1.946 V; 2,160 V -> 2.156 V.\nR801 100 kOhm meets R7: 3.6 V clamped tap into an unpowered OPA388 -> at most 33 uA (abs. max. +-10 mA, SBOS777D 6.1). R801 + C801: 1.6 ms.\nU804 OPA388: Vos 5 uV max (7.5 uV over temperature), IB 350 pA max at 25 C / 400 pA 0-85 C (SBOS777D 6.7) -> 0.4 nA x 150 kOhm = 60 uV = 0.06 V of capacitor\nvoltage. It is a different family (zero-crossover, not chopper) from the main chain's OPA333. An Analog Devices ADA4528-1 was preferred for maker diversity but\nits data sheet could not be retrieved (capture notes).\nR802 1 MOhm to 3V3_SUP: a failed-open follower reads full scale -> OVP trips (a detected, no-shock failure, like §13 fault 16a) instead of hiding an\nover-voltage."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 181.35 17.113)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e903ce04-ef6b-5e7f-a2c8-dc83d91a2fbc")
	)
	(text_box "AD7171 16-bit delta-sigma ADC, 125 Hz, ratiometric to VREF_S (ADR3425)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 227.07 25.4 0)
		(size 140 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d61b02d8-6072-5f8c-b198-3fe6379e2562")
	)
	(text_box "AIN+ = buffered tap through R803 1 k / C803 10 nF C0G; AIN- = GND; REFIN = VREF_S 2.5 V -> full scale 2.5 V = 2,505 V; LSB\n(offset binary, +-VREF) 76.3 uV = 76 mV of capacitor voltage.\nAD7171 average input current 400 nA/V (Rev. C Table 2) -> 0.78 uA x 1 k = 0.78 mV static at 1.95 V: proportional to the\ninput, so it is a gain term removed by calibration; its drift (60 pA/V/K) is 5 uV over 45 K.\nTwo-wire read-only interface: SCLK in (Schmitt), DOUT/RDY out. PDRST low = power-down/reset; R804 100 kOhm pull-down =\ndefault off (contract §5.6). Exposed pad to GND (Table 6).\nDecoupling 100 nF + 1 uF at VDD."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 227.07 31.75 0)
		(size 140 17.113)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "840b6be3-6e15-5531-9b7f-5cf9863fa181")
	)
	(text_box "VREF_S = 2.5 V, ADR3425 (Analog Devices), supervisor chain only"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 387.39 25.4 0)
		(size 172.52 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5e3d63e8-763d-569b-9b33-f17d55bb4686")
	)
	(text_box "ADR3425ARJZ: +-0.1 % initial, 8 ppm/K max, 30 ppm / 1000 h at 50 C, thermal hysteresis 70 ppm, VIN 2.7-5.5 V, dropout 200 mV (Rev. B Table 5). Load:\nAD7171 reference 1 uA, threshold divider 0.1 mA. ENABLE tied to VIN (>= 0.85 VIN). Input 100 nF + 1 uF, output 1 uF + 100 nF (Rev. B 'Input and Output\nCapacitors': 1-10 uF input, 0.1 uF ceramic).\nVREF_S is drawn as a power symbol made here by the reference's power_out pin (contract §4); used on this sheet only."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 387.39 31.75 0)
		(size 172.52 10.636)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "67496a90-f387-503a-b087-6b3d1cfa1c92")
	)
	(text_box "LATCHING over-voltage comparator OVP_TRIP (2,107 V), TLV9031 push-pull on 3V3_SUP (revision 0.3)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 89.503 0)
		(size 166.28 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e218a4c1-1da8-546e-a0b8-322dfc001fd9")
	)
	(text_box "U803 IN- = OVP_REF = VREF_S x 15.6 k / (21.5 k + 15.6 k) = 1.0512 V (0.1 % parts, C810 100 nF). IN+ = OVP_SENSE: R805 100 k from the buffered tap,\nR806 100 k from the output (Rin = Rf).\nTrip (output low before): VCAPS_BUF = 2 x 1.0512 = 2.1024 V -> x 1,002.0 = 2,107 V nominal. Once OVP_TRIP is high (>= 2.1 V is enough) OVP_SENSE\n>= OVP_TRIP / 2 > OVP_REF for any tap >= 0 V: LATCHED.\nBand [CALC, sim/rev3-wpc/ovp_band.py, worst case of every term, -20..+70 C]: 2,071-2,141 V (2,071-2,152 V if 100 nA of Q801 off-state leakage is\nassumed on OVP_SENSE). Bottom 62 V above the top of a normal adult charge (2,008.6 V); top 59 V (48 V) below the 2,200 V rating. Largest term: the\nsupervisor string ratio (+-14 V).\nRelease: ONLY by an OVP_RST rising edge (group ovp_rst) or loss of 3V3_SUP. The issue-2 text (2,160 V, release near 1,000 V) is obsolete (C-5).\nPower-up: TLV9031 SNOSDA3H rev. H deleted the power-on-reset feature, so the output state while 3V3_SUP rises is not guaranteed; powering up\ntripped is the safe direction (both paths forced on, no charge) and firmware clears it with an OVP_RST edge at switch-on (simulated untripped with\nan ideal comparator).\nOutput: push-pull, high = over-voltage -> Q1111 gate on 11 (100 kOhm pull-down there) and the supervisor (R7 receiver on 05). Load <= 0.1 mA: VOH\nwithin 0.1 V of 3V3_SUP. TLV9031 inputs fault-tolerant to 6 V regardless of V+ (SNOSDA3H 5.1).\nUnpowered (3V3_SUP off) -> OVP_TRIP low = no force: accepted latent fault 33; 3V3_SUP off also stops HOLD_S_CLK, so stack B conducts anyway."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 95.853 0)
		(size 166.28 32.226)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5d8e1edf-0f8d-5d99-a7cf-aa184387e132")
	)
	(text_box "OVP_RST: edge-only reset of the latch (C812 100 nF / R809 100 k into Q801 BSS138, 1 k to OVP_SENSE)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 387.39 116.046 0)
		(size 171.32 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "39b37eed-9c02-55f7-b6c7-df9a46f00202")
	)
	(text_box "OVP_RST rising edge -> OVP_RG jumps to 3.3 V and decays with 100 k x 100 nF = 10 ms; Q801 (VGS(th) 0.8-1.5 V at 1 mA, onsemi BSS138/D Rev. 7) conducts\nfor 10 ms x ln(3.3/VGS(th)) = 7.9-14 ms and pulls OVP_SENSE to 3.2 V x 1 k / 101 k = 32 mV < OVP_REF: output low. After the pulse the latch stays clear\nif the capacitor is below the trip, and re-trips at once if it is not.\nA line stuck HIGH cannot hold the latch clear (the gate decays through R809): simulated, sim/rev3-wpc case 'test_with_RST_stuck_high'. A falling edge\ndrives the gate to about -3.3 V (VGS rating +-20 V).\nR811 100 kOhm = contract default resistor (OVP_RST low)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 387.39 122.396 0)
		(size 171.32 14.954)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "652ce8c6-18cb-5429-82f7-85fbfbdafcc3")
	)
	(text_box "OVP_TEST: test injection into the follower INPUT VCAPS_IN (R812 4.7 k + D801 BAS116) - departs from C-4, see note"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 187.799 0)
		(size 194.84 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "caae2d64-df97-57c7-bb01-960cf37b154a")
	)
	(text_box "OVP_TEST high: VCAPS_IN = (OVP_TEST - VF) x 149.8 k / (149.8 k + 4.7 k) = 2.42-2.86 V [CALC: 3V3_SUP 3.2-3.4 V assumed, BAS116 VF 0.45-0.70 V at 15-20 uA EST] -> the\nfollower, R805 and the comparator all see a tap above the trip (top of band 2.133 V at VCAPS_BUF, sheet-08 parts only): trips within about 0.1 ms. 149.8 k = R801 100 k +\nthe string's tap source on 11 (10 k + 39.8 k).\nDEPARTURE from change order C-4 (which injects at OVP_SENSE through 22 k): injecting after R805 leaves a single-part fault hidden: R805 open (the real tap can no longer\nreach the comparator, but the injected test still trips and latches) - simulated, sim/rev3-wpc case arr2_R805_open. Injecting at VCAPS_IN makes the test pass only through\nU804, R805 and U803; R801 open or C801 short is seen by the main/supervisor reading comparison as before.\nSide effects: during the test the supervisor's own ADC reads full scale (> 2,500 V) - firmware must expect that in T-6 and not log it as a disagreement; VCAP_S_TAP on 11\nrises to about 0.8 V (well inside its 3.6 V clamp).\nOVP_TEST low: D801 is reverse biased by VCAPS_IN (<= 2.2 V); leakage <= 5 nA (BAS116LT1/D Rev. 14, 75 V 25 C) x 150 k = 0.75 mV = 0.75 V of reading (80 nA absolute bound at\n150 C -> 12 V; at 70 C and 2 V far less [EST]).\nR813 100 kOhm = contract default resistor (OVP_TEST low)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 194.149 0)
		(size 194.84 25.749)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "443e16ed-c406-5d27-9e24-51de1c34073f")
	)
